# QA session results

> **This is a draft.** The `.draft` suffix keeps `apply_results.py` from seeing it —
> the script globs `RESULTS/*.md`, and a half-filled file it picks up gets recorded
> as *applied* even when it contains no verdicts, which would mean it is never
> applied again once you do fill it in.
>
> **When the Result column is filled:** rename to `2026-08-14-caleb.md`, run
> `python3 Tools/QA/apply_results.py --dry-run` and check your row appears, then tell
> Claude *"my QA results are in `Docs/QA/RESULTS/2026-08-14-caleb.md` — apply them."*
> Full instructions: `Docs/QA/README.md` § "For QA — how to run a session".
>
> `Result` must be spelled exactly `PASS` / `FAIL` / `PARTIAL` / `BLOCKED` / `SKIP`.
> Anything else is silently dropped. Never delete the `qa-results-table` markers —
> they are what stops the scratch notes below from being parsed as verdicts.

